# Round 18, C1-17 (follows). L §4.1 `by n` no longer gives a key a law date ("Its law date is its first day" is gone);
# L §4.3: "A period is not a law date. at m with m a month is refused (LOAD-LAWPERIOD)". A key of a month range by 3
# (a quarter, L §4.1) is a month: `at q` is refused.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index qs = month 2026-01..2026-12 by 3
input fee: money PLN
def f[q in qs]: money PLN = fee at q
version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  fee = 5
ask a: f[2026-04]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWPERIOD at q: a period is not a law date (m.tally:10)
